#
# Counter-example for math:ProofDependencyGraphAnchoredConstraint: a
# math:ProofDependencyGraph that names no math:Proof through math:dependencyGraphOf. A
# lifted declaration DAG underlying no proof is a set of edges with nothing derived at
# the end of them, so the goal-decomposed reading the proof bridge frames has no target;
# that is the graph-side residue of the front-end's math:IllFoundedProofDerivation
# refusal. The class's own definition already names the proof it underlies, so without
# this constraint the naming is prose only and the DAG floats unattached.
#
# The class carries no OWL frame of its own, so the unanchored node IS the whole
# violation and nothing further is needed to isolate it. It fires
# math:ProofDependencyGraphAnchoredConstraint (shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent →
# math:IllFoundedProofDerivation).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/proof-dependency-graph-unanchored/> .

ex:dag a math:ProofDependencyGraph .
